    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d761">

                <pb facs="1034" n="918" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg918"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.6463/89: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominion Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-01-26T12:00:00-04:40"><hi rendition="#italic">January 26,
                                1923—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received January 27—9:50
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2. Interview with the Minister of the Interior this morning and he stated to me
                    confidentially that during his term of office nothing will be done to dispossess
                    Light and Power Company of its properties and requests me to say that he thinks
                    Mr. Hunt<anchor n="12" xml:id="d761-f1"/> should come here at once fully
                    empowered to negotiate sale of plant or sign new contract for service of water
                    and light.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d761-f1" n="12" xml:id="d761-f1-content">
                <p>A. F. Hunt, Jr., the company’s attorney.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
